d2d1: Draw consecutive primitives with the same state and constants together.

Each primitive was its own upload and draw call, and its own draw on
wined3d's command thread. While Affinity drags a selection it draws
about 540 primitives a frame, half of them with the same shape type,
solid brush and constants as the one before.

Collect such primitives, with their indices rebased, and upload and
draw them together. Only solid brushes are batched (nothing to bind),
and the constants are compared by their place in the constant ring,
which is only reused while they are unchanged. The batch is drawn
before anything that changes other state or uses the target: a
constant ring map (which also covers a ring discard), any other draw,
a clip change, GetDC, CopyFromRenderTarget, and
d2d_device_context_end_batch(), which runs at BeginDraw, EndDraw,
Flush, SetTarget and before another context draws on the device.
WINE_D2D_NO_DRAW_BATCHING=1 turns it off.

Affinity, three alternating rounds: dragging a selection, 4% more
frames, wined3d's command thread -40% and the UI thread -5% per frame;
node editing, 6% more frames, -43% and -11%; zooming, -29% and -10%.
The d2d1 conformance tests give the same results, and the canvas is
pixel identical with and without a selection.
